# Conventional Commits

When creating git commits in this repository, use Conventional Commits:

- `feat`: new user-facing capability
- `fix`: bug fix
- `refactor`: change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
- `docs`: documentation only
- `style`: formatting/whitespace with no behavior change
- `test`: adding or updating tests
- `chore`: tooling, deps, config, or other non-product work
- `perf`: performance improvement

Format: `<type>(optional-scope): <short description>`

Rules:

- Imperative mood, lowercase description, no trailing period
- Keep the subject to about 72 characters
- Use a body only when needed for context
- Examples: `feat(cart): apply coupon codes at checkout`, `fix(product): show back link to catalog`
